# SAGE

Spec-first, AI-assisted development workflow.

When the user types `@sage <command>`, load the corresponding rule file:

| Command | Rule file |
|---|---|
| `@sage spec <description>` | `.cursor/rules/sage-spec.mdc` |
| `@sage behavior` | `.cursor/rules/sage-behavior.mdc` |
| `@sage code` | `.cursor/rules/sage-code.mdc` |
| `@sage update <feedback>` | `.cursor/rules/sage-update.mdc` |
| `@sage pr` | `.cursor/rules/sage-pr.mdc` |
| `@sage doc` | `.cursor/rules/sage-doc.mdc` |
| `@sage harness init` | `.cursor/rules/sage-harness-init.mdc` |
| `@sage harness generate` | `.cursor/rules/sage-harness-generate.mdc` |
| `@sage harness review` | `.cursor/rules/sage-harness-review.mdc` |

The harness lives in `.sage/harness.md`. Always load it as context for every SAGE command.
If it doesn't exist, remind the user once and proceed without it.
